+reply stays byte-identical to serial decoding, sampled requests included; the settings travel in the request
+header from rank 0, so both Sparks make the same choice. Not applied where `auto` runs `fc5:0.3` alone (EXL3
+checkpoint with BF16 non-expert weights) or on a checkpoint without the MTP head (`lN` then runs `fc5:0.3`).
 
 `--mtp-drafts N` sets a fixed default, `--no-drafts` serves serially, and `"draft": false` in a request decodes
 that one serially (the reference the drafted replies equal). `"ignore_eos": true` decodes `max_tokens` tokens
